            "days_to_patch": null,
            "description": "<p>National Vulnerability Database has provided the following description: <br /><em>Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection') vulnerability in Pandora FMS on all allows SQL Injection.\u00a0This ulnerability allowed SQL injections to be made even if authentication failed.This issue affects Pandora FMS: from 700 through &lt;776.</em></p>",
            "epss": null,
            "executive_summary": "<ul><li>An Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection') vulnerability exists that, when exploited, allows a privileged attacker to achieve unknown impacts.</li><li>We are currently unaware of exploitation activity in the wild, and exploit code is not publicly available.</li><li>Mandiant Intelligence considers this a Medium-risk vulnerability due to unknown impacts.</li><li>There are currently no mitigation options available for this issue.</li></ul>",
